#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179959 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "976e05d4-59a8-5a93-be2f-b22357f388b9" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Circulation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "553c3284-1cc8-5cd6-bf53-43e787406d04" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8π" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186177755} {:answer/id #uuid "6492d3b1-fbd2-5113-a984-3816de854e5f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4π" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186177756} {:answer/id #uuid "67cdb085-05c1-5c1d-a6f0-ebab6a3d0019" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4π" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186177757} {:answer/id #uuid "6e8ca0af-0e24-5ef6-be62-3bc3b0bcb776" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186177758} {:answer/id #uuid "71e7bf95-6f9c-59a9-8bf1-fa297751aed2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8π" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186177759}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "553c3284-1cc8-5cd6-bf53-43e787406d04" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8π" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186177755} :answer-field/id #uuid "c3dc50a4-262e-58bd-857d-bd66b3231b7a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186177754}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "81113ee4-2843-5316-a3de-8f3bdbd20c2b" :question/math-academy-id "q-125485" :question/problem "Calculate the circulation $Γ$ of the vector field $F(x,y)=\\frac{5}{y}\\,i+\\frac{1}{x}\\,j$ along the ellipse $C$ with equation $25{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=25$ oriented counterclockwise. Interpret circulation as the sum of four convergent improper line integrals over the open quadrant arcs, with independent one-sided limits at $(\\pm1,0)$ and $(0,\\pm5)$. The field is undefined at those four points, so the original ordinary circulation is not defined." :question/worked-solution "The original field is undefined at the four axis intersections, so an ordinary line integral over the whole ellipse is not defined. For the explicit improper interpretation, $r(t)=(\\cos t,5\\sin t)$ traverses $25x^2+y^2=25$ counterclockwise. On each open quadrant arc,\n\n$$\\frac{5}{y}\\,dx=\\frac{5}{5\\sin t}(-\\sin t)\\,dt=-dt,\\qquad\\frac{1}{x}\\,dy=\\frac{1}{\\cos t}(5\\cos t)\\,dt=5dt.$$\n\nThus the scalar pullback is $4$. Each endpoint has the finite one-sided limit $4$, so each open-arc integral converges absolutely and equals $2\\pi$. Their sum is $\\Gamma_{\\mathrm{imp}}=8\\pi$, the unchanged option c. No principal-value cancellation is used, and $F$ remains undefined at the excluded points."}]}
